It is the lunch break.
I walk into a mobile phone shop.
I need a SIM card for my mobile phone.
A clerk is standing there.
"Good afternoon."
"Are you looking for something?" asks the clerk.
"Good afternoon," I answer.
"I need a German SIM card," I say.
"Do you have an address in Germany?" he asks.
"Yes, I have an address now," I answer.
I have the registration in my bag.
"Very good."
"I need your passport and your registration," says the clerk.
I open my bag.
"Here are my passport and my registration," I say.
He takes the papers.
He looks at the registration.
"Thank you."
"Frau Flores."
"Do you work here in Berlin?" he asks.
"Yes, I work here as a software engineer," I answer.
"Welcome to Berlin," the clerk says kindly.
